        <div id="types" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Guest Bed, Camping Airbed or Classic Low Mattress: Which Air Mattress Do You Need?
          </h2>

          <p>
            The best air mattress depends on where it will be used. A bed that lives in a hall closet for holidays needs different things from one that goes in the car for a weekend at a state park. Almost every air mattress on Amazon falls into one of three groups, and knowing which group you need narrows the choice faster than comparing brands.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Raised Guest Beds With Built-In Pumps</h3>

          <p>
            Raised beds, sometimes called double-high or high-rise airbeds, stand roughly 16 to 22 inches tall and have an electric pump built into the side. The SoundAsleep Dream Series, King Koil, Intex Dura-Beam Comfort Plush and Intex Dura-Beam Deluxe twin all fit here. They are the best air mattress for guests because they sit at about the height of a regular bed, inflate with the turn of a dial and can be topped up in seconds. The catch is that they need a wall outlet and take up more closet space.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Camping Air Mattresses</h3>

          <p>
            Camping airbeds are lower, usually 8 to 12 inches, so they fit under a tent roof and pack smaller. The best camping air mattress inflates without mains power, either with a battery pump like the Bestway Tritech's or a hand pump like the one in the Intex Classic Downy set. Some double-high beds, such as the Coleman SupportRest, are sold for camping too, but they suit campsites with electric hookups.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Classic Low Airbeds</h3>

          <p>
            The classic airbed is a single flocked layer with no pump inside. It is the cheapest and most compact option and works as a backup bed, a sleepover mattress or a camping bed. It is also the least convenient, because you need a separate pump and it sits on the floor.
          </p>
        </div>

