          </h2>

          <p>
            The pump decides how easy an air mattress is to live with, and it is the spec most buyers overlook. Inflation times below are the makers' figures; real times vary with the pump, the room temperature and how firm you like the bed.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Built-In 120V Electric Pumps</h3>

          <p>
            A built-in AC pump is the most convenient design: plug it in, turn the dial and the bed fills itself. Listed inflation times for our raised queens range from about 2 minutes for the King Koil to under 4 minutes for the SoundAsleep and about 4.75 minutes for the 22-inch Intex. Twins are quicker, such as about 2.25 minutes for the Intex Deluxe twin. The same pump deflates the bed and lets you add a little air before bed without dragging out a separate pump.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Built-In Battery Pumps</h3>

          <p>
            A battery pump works anywhere. The Bestway Tritech's built-in pump runs on four D-cell batteries and is listed at 3 minutes for a queen. It is the best air mattress with a built-in pump for camping, as long as you remember fresh batteries.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Hand and Separate Pumps</h3>

